        "text": "You are a chef."
      }
    ]
  }
}
</code></pre> Step 2: Request a batch prediction job <p></p> <p>Specify your BigQuery input table, model, and output location to create a batch prediction job.</p> <p>Troubleshooting</p> <p>If you encounter issues with code snippets or setup, refer to the Troubleshooting Guide.</p> RESTGen AI SDK for Python <p>To create a batch prediction job, use the <code>projects.locations.batchPredictionJobs.create</code> method.</p> <p>Before using any of the request data, make the following replacements:</p> <ul> <li><code>LOCATION</code>: A region that supports Gemini models.</li> <li><code>PROJECT_ID</code>: Your project ID.</li> <li><code>MODEL_PATH</code>: The publisher model name (e.g., <code>publishers/google/models/gemini-2.0-flash-001</code>) or the tuned endpoint name (e.g., <code>projects/PROJECT_ID/locations/LOCATION/models/MODEL_ID</code>).</li> <li><code>INPUT_URI</code>: The BigQuery table location (e.g., <code>bq://myproject.mydataset.input_table</code>). Multi-region datasets are not supported.</li> <li><code>OUTPUT_FORMAT</code>: <code>bigquery</code> for BigQuery output or <code>jsonl</code> for Cloud Storage output.</li> <li><code>DESTINATION</code>: <code>bigqueryDestination</code> for BigQuery or <code>gcsDestination</code> for Cloud Storage.</li> <li><code>OUTPUT_URI_FIELD_NAME</code>: <code>outputUri</code> for BigQuery or <code>outputUriPrefix</code> for Cloud Storage.</li> <li><code>OUTPUT_URI</code>: The BigQuery table (e.g., <code>bq://myproject.mydataset.output_result</code>) or the Cloud Storage bucket and directory (e.g., <code>gs://mybucket/path/to/output</code>).</li> </ul> <p>HTTP method and URL:</p> <pre><code>POST https://LOCATION-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1/projects/PROJECT_ID/locations/LOCATION/batchPredictionJobs
</code></pre> <p>Request JSON body:</p> <pre><code>{
