Expand to see all prerequisites Concepts <ul> <li>RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation): A method that enhances LLM responses by retrieving relevant information from an external knowledge base.</li> <li>Vector Database: A database designed to store and query high-dimensional vectors, commonly used for similarity searches.</li> <li>Embedding Model: A model that converts text or other data into numerical vector representations (embeddings).</li> <li>Secret Manager: A Google Cloud service for securely storing and managing secrets like API keys, passwords, and certificates.</li> <li>Hybrid Search: A search technique that combines keyword-based (sparse vector) and semantic (dense vector) search methods to improve result relevance.</li> </ul> <p>1. Set up your Weaviate database</p> <p>Before using the Weaviate database with RAG Engine, you must provision your Weaviate instance.</p> <ul> <li>Create and deploy your Weaviate database instance and collection. You can follow the Weaviate official quickstart guide or optionally use the Google Cloud Marketplace guide. You are responsible for managing your Weaviate database instance lifecycle.</li> <li>Prepare an HTTPS endpoint. While HTTP is supported, an HTTPS connection between RAG Engine and your Weaviate database is recommended.</li> <li> <p>Create a Weaviate collection with the required schema. RAG Engine requires a one-to-one mapping between a RAG corpus and a Weaviate collection. Use the following schema when creating your collection:</p> Property name Data type <code>fileId</code> <code>text</code> <code>corpusId</code> <code>text</code> <code>chunkId</code> <code>text</code> <code>chunkDataType</code> <code>text</code> <code>chunkData</code> <code>text</code> <code>fileOriginalUri</code> <code>text</code> </li> <li> <p>Create a Weaviate API key. RAG Engine uses an API key for authentication and authorization. Follow the Weaviate authentication guide to configure API key-based authentication.</p> </li> </ul> <p>2. Set up your Google Cloud project</p> <ol> <li>Sign in to your Google Cloud account. If you're new to Google Cloud, create an account to evaluate how our products perform in real-world scenarios. New customers also get $300 in free credits to run, test, and deploy workloads.</li> <li> <p>In the Google Cloud console, on the project selector page, select or create a Google Cloud project.</p> <p>Note</p> <p>If you don't plan to keep the resources that you create in this procedure, create a project instead of selecting an existing project. After you finish these steps, you can delete the project, removing all resources associated with the project.</p> <p>Go to project selector</p> </li> <li> <p>Enable the Vertex AI and Secret Manager APIs.</p> <p>Enable the APIs</p> </li> <li> <p>In the Google Cloud console, activate Cloud Shell.</p> <p>Activate Cloud Shell</p> <p>At the bottom of the Google Cloud console, a Cloud Shell session starts and displays a command-line prompt. Cloud Shell is a shell environment with the Google Cloud CLI already installed and with values already set for your current project. It can take a few seconds for the session to initialize.</p> </li> </ol> <p>3. Store your Weaviate API key in Secret Manager</p> <p>To protect your API key, store it in Secret Manager and grant the RAG Engine service account access to it.</p> <ol> <li>Store your Weaviate API key in Google Cloud Secret Manager.</li> <li>Grant your project's RAG Engine service account permissions to access the secret. The service account is created automatically when you create your first RAG resource and has the format <code>service-{project-number}@gcp-sa-vertex-rag.iam.gserviceaccount.com</code>.<ol> <li>Navigate to your project's IAM &amp; Admin page.</li> <li>Enable the option Include Google-provided role grants.</li> <li>Find the service account and grant it the Secret Manager Secret Accessor (<code>roles/secretmanager.secretAccessor</code>) role.</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <p>4. Authenticate and install clients</p> <p>Set up authentication and install the necessary client libraries for your chosen development environment.</p> PythonNode.jsJavaGoC#REST API <ol> <li> <p>If you're using a local shell, create local authentication credentials for your user account:</p> <pre><code>gcloud auth application-default login
