Google Cloud consoleVertex AI API <p>You can enable the layout parser when creating a new corpus in the Google Cloud console.</p> Steps to import files using the Google Cloud console <ol> <li> <p>In the Google Cloud console, go to the RAG Engine page.</p> <p>Go to RAG Engine</p> </li> <li> <p>Select Create corpus.</p> </li> <li>In the Region field, select your region.</li> <li>In the Corpus name field, enter a name for your corpus.</li> <li>In the Description field, enter a description.</li> <li>In the Data section, select the source of your data.</li> <li>Expand the Advanced options section.<ul> <li>In the Chunking strategy section, the following default sizes are recommended:<ul> <li>Chunking size: 1024</li> <li>Chunk overlap: 256</li> </ul> </li> <li>In the Layout parser section, select the LLM parser option.<ol> <li>From the Model field, select your model.</li> <li>Optional: In the Maximum parsing requests per min field, enter your maximum parsing requests.</li> <li>Optional: In the Custom parsing prompt field, enter your parsing prompt.</li> <li>Click Continue.</li> </ol> </li> </ul> </li> <li>On the Configure vector store page, do the following:<ol> <li>In the Embedding model field, select your embedding model.</li> <li>In the Vector database section, select your database.</li> </ol> </li> <li>Click Create corpus.</li> </ol> <p>You can use the <code>ImportRagFiles</code> method in the Vertex AI API to import files and apply the layout parser programmatically.</p> <p>Troubleshooting</p> <p>If you encounter issues with code snippets or setup, refer to the Troubleshooting Guide.</p> PythonREST <p>To learn how to install or update the Vertex AI SDK for Python, see Install the Vertex AI SDK for Python. For more information, see the Python API reference documentation.</p> <p>Before running the sample, replace the following variables: *   <code>PROJECT_ID</code>: Your project ID. *   <code>LOCATION</code>: The region to process the request (for example, <code>us-central1</code>). *   <code>RAG_CORPUS_ID</code>: The ID of your RAG corpus. *   <code>GCS_URIS</code>: A list of Cloud Storage URIs (for example, <code>["gs://my-bucket1", "gs://my-bucket2"]</code>). *   <code>LAYOUT_PARSER_PROCESSOR_NAME</code>: The full resource name of your layout parser processor (for example, <code>"projects/{project}/locations/{location}/processors/{processor_id}"</code>).</p> <pre><code>from vertexai import rag
import vertexai

# TODO(developer):- Update these variables before running the sample.
PROJECT_ID = "your-project-id"
LOCATION = "us-central1"
RAG_CORPUS_ID = "your-rag-corpus-id"
GCS_URIS = ["gs://your-bucket/your-files-dir"]
LAYOUT_PARSER_PROCESSOR_NAME = "projects/your-project-id/locations/us-central1/processors/your-processor-id"

# Initialize Vertex AI API
vertexai.init(project=PROJECT_ID, location=LOCATION)

response = rag.import_files(
    corpus_name=f"projects/{PROJECT_ID}/locations/{LOCATION}/ragCorpora/{RAG_CORPUS_ID}",
    paths=GCS_URIS,
    chunk_size=1024,  # Optional
    chunk_overlap=256,  # Optional
    parsing_config=rag.ParsingConfig(
        layout_parser=rag.LayoutParser(processor_name=LAYOUT_PARSER_PROCESSOR_NAME)
    ),
)
print(f"Imported {response.imported_rag_files_count} files.")
</code></pre> <p>The following sample shows how to import Cloud Storage files using the layout parser. For more configuration options, see the <code>ImportRagFilesConfig</code> reference.</p> <p>Before using the request data, replace the following variables: *   <code>PROJECT_ID</code>: Your project ID. *   <code>LOCATION</code>: The region to process the request (for example, <code>us-central1</code>). *   <code>RAG_CORPUS_ID</code>: The ID of your RAG corpus. *   <code>GCS_URIS</code>: A list of Cloud Storage URIs (for example, <code>["gs://my-bucket1", "gs://my-bucket2"]</code>). *   <code>LAYOUT_PARSER_PROCESSOR_NAME</code>: The full resource name of your layout parser processor (for example, <code>"projects/{project}/locations/{location}/processors/{processor_id}"</code>). *   <code>CHUNK_SIZE</code>: The number of tokens each chunk should have (for example, <code>1024</code>).</p> <p>HTTP request: <pre><code>POST https://LOCATION-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1/projects/PROJECT_ID/locations/LOCATION/ragCorpora/RAG_CORPUS_ID/ragFiles:import
</code></pre></p> <p>Request JSON body: <pre><code>{
  "importRagFilesConfig": {
    "gcsSource": {
      "uris": GCS_URIS
    },
    "ragFileParsingConfig": {
      "layoutParser": {
        "processorName": "LAYOUT_PARSER_PROCESSOR_NAME"
      }
