Before you begin Concepts <ul> <li>Model Garden: A curated platform in Vertex AI for discovering, testing, and deploying foundation models.</li> <li>Vertex AI Endpoint: A service that makes a deployed model available for online prediction requests.</li> <li>TPU (Tensor Processing Unit): Google's custom-developed accelerator for machine learning workloads, optimized for large-scale training and inference.</li> <li>Gemma: A family of lightweight, state-of-the-art open models from Google.</li> <li>Instruction-tuned model: A model that has been further fine-tuned on examples of instructions and their desired outputs to improve its ability to follow user commands.</li> </ul> <p>Set up a Google Cloud project</p> <ol> <li>Sign in to your Google Cloud account. If you're new to Google Cloud, create an account to evaluate how our products perform in real-world scenarios. New customers also get $300 in free credits to run, test, and deploy workloads.</li> <li> <p>In the Google Cloud console, on the project selector page, select or create a Google Cloud project.</p> <p>Note: If you don't plan to keep the resources that you create in this procedure, create a project instead of selecting an existing project. After you finish these steps, you can delete the project, removing all resources associated with the project.</p> <p>Go to project selector</p> </li> <li> <p>Make sure that billing is enabled for your Google Cloud project.</p> </li> <li> <p>Enable the Vertex AI API.</p> <p>Enable the API</p> </li> </ol> <p>Set up your local environment</p> <ol> <li> <p>Install and initialize the Google Cloud CLI.</p> </li> <li> <p>If you previously installed the gcloud CLI, ensure your <code>gcloud</code> components are updated by running this command.</p> <pre><code>gcloud components update
